course: dictionary
lesson: 6838
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word outfit can mean a set of clothes, a costume, a group of people, or the clothes and equipment you give someone. To find the right meaning, read the context: the words and sentences around it.
explain: «In Georgia, USA, Faith, one of six, never gets a new outfit: everything's a hand-me-down.» Here outfit means a set of clothes. The clue is hand-me-down: Faith wears clothes that were passed on from someone else.
explain: «In London, Amira and Yasmin, 10, have always had matching outfits.» Matching tells you the girls wear the same clothes. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: An outfit is a set of clothes worn together.
fact: An outfit can also be a costume for a special event, such as a party or a dress-up day.
fact: Informally, an outfit can mean a group, team, band or company.
fact: To outfit someone means to give them the clothes or equipment they need.
fact: A hand-me-down is something, such as clothing, that is passed on from someone else.
exercise: «He liked her outfit.» What does outfit mean here? | To give someone new equipment | A team of workers at a company | *A set of clothes worn together | A tent and a map for a trip
exercise: Ms Ali says the class will wear a cowboy outfit for the show. What does outfit mean? | A group of children who sing together | *A costume for a special event | A new pair of trainers only | A set of tools for science
exercise: The coach will outfit the whole team with new boots and kit. What does outfit mean? | To take off clothes | To cut out a shape from paper | *To give someone the clothes or equipment they need | To shout loudly across a field
test: «The little company is a small outfit run by two sisters.» What does outfit mean here? | A way to get dressed quickly | To fit someone with glasses | *A small business or group | A set of clothes for a party
test: Faith's family has no spare money, so she wears hand-me-downs. What does outfit mean if the sentence is «Faith's outfit was old but clean»? | *A set of clothes worn together | A costume for a play | A team of helpers | To equip a boat
exam: «The school gave every child a dress-up outfit for the show, and the teacher said they would outfit the choir with new capes too.» Which meaning of outfit is used in the first part? | To give someone equipment | A type of hat | A group of people working together | *A costume for a special event
